description:
File: rust/lichen-gateway/src/discovery.rs
Lines: 308-320

Function returns i32 (-1/0/1) C-style comparison instead of std::cmp::Ordering. This forces callers to interpret magic numbers and prevents using .cmp() idioms.

Current:
```rust
pub fn compare_ipv6_iids(a: &[u8; 16], b: &[u8; 16]) -> i32 {
    // ... returns -1, 0, or 1
}
```

Fix:
```rust
pub fn compare_ipv6_iids(a: &[u8; 16], b: &[u8; 16]) -> std::cmp::Ordering {
    let a_val = iid_to_u64(&a[8..16].try_into().unwrap());
    let b_val = iid_to_u64(&b[8..16].try_into().unwrap());
    a_val.cmp(&b_val)
}
```
